      "Language": "swe",
      "Abstract": {"AbstractText": "Parkinson's disease is a relatively common disorder in elderly patients. With carefully performed treatment a considerable improvement can be seen also in patients of high age. L-dopa as well as other antiparkinsonian drugs should be used in lower doses than those subscribed for younger patients. Cognitive decline implies a certain risk for mental confusion, in which case the dose of the causing agent has to be lowered or the treatment interrupted."},
